    "result_text": "The full test suite passes: **265 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**, BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds a computed `displayName` field (formatted `LastName, FirstName`) to the owner response.\n\n**Implementation** (two edits):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `displayName` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field (getter/setter) and it is serialized in every owner response.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct mapping that computes the value when converting `Owner` \u2192 `OwnerDto`:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\", expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);\n   ```\n\nSince the mapper is used by the shared `RespondWith*` functions, `displayName` is populated on both the create (`POST /api/owners`) and read (`GET /api/owners/{id}`) responses \u2014 which is what the `Cp06Tests` acceptance test verifies (it creates an owner with first name \"John\", then asserts `$.displayName` equals `\"<LastName>, John\"` on the GET). No OfficeFloor pipeline changes were needed since the value is derived purely from existing entity fields at response time.",
